From 453142b4963577dd3f9c8e8dd8a39bc21a529e9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 10:24:32 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(post): probe positioning moves post as protected
 stop-on-contact moves

The descent from the rapid / safe plane to each touch's start, the bore
entry and the rise of a probe cycle were plain G01 feeds: a part or
clamp not where the model says broke the stylus on them. The dump now
marks every non-rapid move of a probe path that is not a touch or its
back-off as a GUARD record (Record::Guard, docs/CNC-INTERMEDIATE.md),
and the engine calls the new onProbeGuard hook for it:

- Fanuc: G31 to the point, then per moving axis
  IF[ABS[#506n-end]GT0.001]THEN#3000=3(PROBE HIT ON POSITIONING) - the
  skip position equals the block end only when no contact came.
- Tormach PathPilot: G38.3 to the point, then o5001 if [#5070 EQ 1] /
  (MSG, PROBE HIT ON POSITIONING) / M2 / o5001 endif (LinuxCNC G-code
  reference: G38.3, #5070, O-codes).

A post script without onProbeGuard is refused by name, once per
operation. An inverted axis mirrors a GUARD like an absolute move.
Pinned by probe_guard (marking, stream round-trip, Fanuc corner golden,
Tormach guard golden, refusal) and the regenerated Fanuc probe goldens.

Fixes #174

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
